[1;1H[1m[;m  [22m[;m                                                                              [2;1H[1m[;m  [;m# CODE Git kernel freeze clarifications — R2[22m                                  [3;1H[1m[;m  [22m[;m                                                                              [4;1H[1m[;m  [;mArchitect supplement to the unchanged CODE-GIT-KERNEL-R1.md, addressing the[22m   [5;1H[1m[;m  [;mfour[22m                                                                          [6;1H[1m[;m  [;mminor contract findings in `E/code-git-kernel-contract-review-r1.json`. The[22m   [7;1H[1m[;m  [;mexact[22m                                                                         [8;1H[1m[;m  [;mworkspace and immutable fixture remain bound by the separate freeze record.[22m   [9;1H[1m[;m  [22m[;m                                                                              [10;1H[1m[;m  [;m## Helpers[22m                                                                    [11;1H[1m[;m  [22m[;m                                                                              [12;1H[1m[;m  [;mBoth helpers raise the same CodeGitProofError, exit_code=2. For[22m               [13;1H[1m[;m  [;mgit_object_ids,[22m                                                               [14;1H[1m[;m  [;mvalidation order is object_format, object_type, body type, then body byte cap.[15;1H[;m  [;mframe_git_object follows the same order without object_format. A bad exact[22m    [16;1H[1m[;m  [;mtype[22m                                                                          [17;1H[1m[;m  [;mor unsupported enum uses CODE_PROOF_INPUT_INVALID with instance_pointer[22m       [18;1H[1m[;m  [;mexactly[22m                                                                       [19;1H[1m[;m  [;m`/object_format`, `/object_type` or `/body`, and a bounded reason string.[22m     [20;1H[1m[;m  [22m[;m                