[1;1H[2m┃[22m◆ [1m[2mThought[22m[2m for 50.7s[22m                                                            [2;1H[2m┃[22m                                                                               [3;1H[2m┃[3mThere's a potential issue: [1m_load_fixture()[22m[2m runs at import time, which is fine.[23m[22m [4;1H[2m┃[3mBut [1mtest_kernel_call_does_not_use_io_or_network[22m[2m calls [1m_verify_case[22m[2m which uses[23m[22m  [5;1H[2m┃[3mFIXTURE already loaded. I understand the concerns about the test setup and[23m[22m     [6;1H[2m┃[3mpotential side effects in [1m_minimal_graph[22m[2m and [1m_verify_case[22m[2m. Let me address the[23m[22m  [7;1H[2m┃[3mspecific issues you've raised.[23m[22m                                                 [8;1H[2m┃[22m                                                                               [9;1H[2m┃[3mThe key points are:[23m[22m                                                            [10;1H[2m┃[3m1. [1m_load_fixture()[22m[2m runs at import time - that's intentional for the frozen[23m[22m     [11;1H[2m┃[3mcontract[23m[22m                                                                       [12;1H[2m┃[3m2. [1mtest_kernel_call_does_not_use io_or_network[22m[2m - the guard is properly applied[23m[22m [13;1H[2m┃[3mbefore verification[23m[22m                                                            [14;1H[2m┃[3m3. [1m_minimal_graph[22m[2m calls [1mgit_object_ids[22m[2m during setup - that's expected and[23m[22m      [15;1H[2m┃[3mcontrolled[23m[22m                                                                     [16;1H[2m┃[3m4. The size cap test modification - we need to ensure we re-sort after changing[17;1H[23m┃[3mOIDs to maintain consistency[23m[22m                                                   [18;1H[2m┃[22m                                                                               [19;1H[2m┃[3mFor the test bug in [1mtest_size and_hash_mismatch_and_body_key_set[22m[2m, you're right[23m[22m [20;1H[2m┃[3mthat mutating [1mobjects[0]["oid"][22m[2m can break the sorting and commit_oid matching.[23m[22m [21;1H[2m┃[3mThe cleaner approach is:[23m[22m                                                       [22;1H[2m┃[22m                                                                               [23;1H[2m┃[3m• Keep the record's oid as the key in bodies[23m[22m                                   [24;1H[2m┃[3m• Change the declared oid to wrong value[23m[22m                                       [m[m[m[0m[24;1H























